{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Any evil thing, for it is an abomination</b> — to restrain yourself. Everyone who pollutes his mouth is called an abomination and hated:" "<b>Any evil thing</b> — and written after it: \"a man or a woman who does the evil…\" and goes and serves other elohim — to teach that speech and thought concerning idolatry combine with the deed:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The opening word לוסר is obscure; read as לסור ('to turn aside/restrain'), yielding 'to restrain yourself.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:51.437421809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}